<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Wrigley.jpg" alt="A portrait of a black lab with blue-gray background" width="400" height="397" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Wrigley. 18"x18", oil on linen. 2013.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A commissioned portrait of Wrigley. &nbsp;I took the reference photos on a sunny day in her back yard. &nbsp;She is a very photogenic lady and we had plenty of shots that would have been suitable for a painting. &nbsp;In the end we chose the one that showed off all her best features, especially the ears, eyes and mouth.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I designed the edges to give the painting extra depth and keep the focus on her head. &nbsp;In keeping with a lot of the paintings I've done this year, I used a limited palette of ultramarine blue, viridian (which is where most of the blues actually come from), alizarin crimson, bright red, cadmium yellow light and burnt sienna.</p>